l-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:\n  Line 28: | `allow-list.json` | Keeps the four `command-spec-kit-*` bridge ids for `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:implement`, `/speckit:complete` and `/speckit:resume`. The deriver keeps these rows in place of the matching metadata entries. | Authored input |\n\n  Line 40: allow-list.json + scoring-compatibility.json\n\n  Line 90: Humans may edit `allow-list.json`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `scoring-compatibility.json` and `shadow-diff.md`. Regenerate `command-bridges.generated.json` after changing an authored input or the deriver. Do not edit the generated JSON directly.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts:\n  Line 114: const ALLOW_LIST_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'allow-list.json');\n\n  Line 249:       source: 'scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json',\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/sk-prompt/008-sk-prompt-standalone-conversion/008-docs-and-final-gate/spec.md:\n  Line 91: | advisor `skill_advisor.py`, `allow-list.json`, golden-prompt fixture | Modify | Owner mode and expected mode now name the surviving skill |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/sk-prompt/008-sk-prompt-standalone-conversion/008-docs-and-final-gate/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 74: | advisor `skill_advisor.py`, `allow-list.json`, golden-prompt fixture | Modify | Owner mode and expected mode now name the surviving skill |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/sk-doc/authoring-modes-and-playbooks/002-create-goal-mode/011-cross-surface-references/plan.md:\n  Line 59: - **Command-bridge deriver**: reads each skill's `command-metadata.json` plus `allow-list.json` and `scoring-compatibility.json`, then writes the generated JSON and the generated blocks in the TypeScript and Python scorers.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md:\n  Line 64: 1. **Inventory.** Commands are described by three sources, `command-metadata.json` in three hubs, the bridge `allow-list.json` and `doctor/_routes.yaml`. Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what one drift-proof inventory needs.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/synthesis-review.md:\n  Line 28: | C6 | Three bridge names have no command file | CONFIRMED | `bridges/allow-list.json:32`, `:39`, `:46`, `:53` |\n\n  Line 30: | C8 | Ten command strings carry more than one bridge id, all doctor routes | WRONG | Nine are doctor commands. The tenth is `/memory:save`, with ids `command-memory-save` and `memory:save` (`bridges/allow-list.json:38-50`) |\n\n  Line 136: - **Evidence.** The tree is the only complete source and every mirror generator already reads it (`.codex/SYNC.md:29`, `.pi/SYNC.md:27`, `.dsh/SYNC.md:32`, `.claude/SYNC.md:26`, `.cursor/SYNC.md:32`). The deriver already reads any skill's metadata file (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:78-114`). The allow-list itself says the rows exist because \"system-spec-kit owns the live planning command but has no command-metadata.json yet\" (`bridges/allow-list.json:7`). C54 shows why registries cannot be the second source.\n\n  Line 245: - **Change.** Once the two new metadata files exist, delete all eight rows of `bridges/allow-list.json`, then the file. That removes `/spec_kit`, `/memory:save` and `/prompt`. The same change must update `explicit.ts:95-99` and `:174-175`, the Python table, `AGENTS.md:89` and any corpus row whose gold label is a retired id.\n\n  Line 246: - **Evidence.** C6. Every allow-list reason says the row exists for want of a metadata file (`allow-list.json:7`, `:14`, `:21`, `:28`, `:42`).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/resource-map.md:\n  Line 142: | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json | Cited | OK | Citations=2; Iterations=2 |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md:\n  Line 220: ### Putting the policy in `AGENTS.md` as a second list: there are already four hand-maintained sources (three metadata hubs, `allow-list.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `scoring-compatibility.json`); a fifth would drift the same way. -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\n\n  Line 221: - What was tried: Putting the policy in `AGENTS.md` as a second list: there are already four hand-maintained sources (three metadata hubs, `allow-list.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `scoring-compatibility.json`); a fifth would drift the same way.\n\n  Line 223: - Do NOT retry: Putting the policy in `AGENTS.md` as a second list: there are already four hand-maintained sources (three metadata hubs, `allow-list.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `scoring-compatibility.json`); a fifth would drift the same way.\n\n  Line 292: - Putting the policy in `AGENTS.md` as a second list: there are already four hand-maintained sources (three metadata hubs, `allow-list.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `scoring-compatibility.json`); a fifth would drift the same way. (iteration 4)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/resource-map.md:\n  Line 92: | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json | Cited | OK | Citations=1; Iterations=1 |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md:\n  Line 24: 5. No non-doctor source declares risk at all: `mutating` appears in none of the three `command-metadata.json` files, and `allow-list.json` carries only a free-text `reason` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:1]. The deriver's `readOnly` path is therefore starved for the other 28 commands because the data was never authored, not because the mechanism is missing.\n\n  Line 40: - Putting the policy in `AGENTS.md` as a second list: there are already four hand-maintained sources (three metadata hubs, `allow-list.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `scoring-compatibility.json`); a fifth would drift the same way.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:\n  Line 18: 2. The bridge inventory is generated by summing three sources — 19 entries from the three hub `command-metadata.json` files, 8 from `allow-list.json`, and 35 from `doctor/_routes.yaml` — for 62 entries covering 43 distinct command strings [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:1]. The `counts` block states this explicitly: `commandMetadata: 19, allowList: 8, doctorRoutes: 35, generated: 62` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:1].\n\n  Line 22: 4. Five shipped commands have no bridge entry under their own command string: `/local-skilled-alignment`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:handoff`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search` [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:1]. `/prompt:improve` is reachable only through the legacy `/prompt` id in the allow-list, whose own `reason` field says the Python scorer \"still recognizes legacy /prompt while JSON declares /prompt:improve\" [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:51].\n\n  Line 24: 5. Three bridge commands have no command file at all: `/memory:save` (two ids: `command-memory-save` and `memory:save`), `/prompt`, and the deprecated `/spec_kit` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:37]. The allow-list's `/spec_kit` reason says the deprecated generic bridge \"remains live for one-release compatibility\", and `command-memory-save` reasons that `system-spec-kit` \"has no command-metadata.json yet\" [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:41].\n\n  Line 61: - .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/pi-deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md:\n  Line 33: Which workflows never load their named mode `SKILL.md`: 27 of 45 reference no skill at all, and even inside the 19 metadata entries the declared choreography is not carried by the command file. Should a skill recommendation imply its command: **no**. Implication in that direction is unsound on two counted cases (one dangling `ownerMode`, one mislabelled) and on 27 commands with no linkage at all. The sound direction is the reverse: the command declares `ownerSkillId` (the data exists in `allow-list.json` as `skillId` and in metadata as `ownerMode`), and the advisor surfaces the command with its owner skill attached, so the recommendation is command-first and the skill is context rather than an inference step.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfaci