 generated bridge inventory, allow-list.json or render.ts.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which of the 45 commands in .skilled/commands have an active advisor bridge, which bridges point at retired or unmatched names, and what would one drift-proof inventory require?\",\"Why do plain planning and research prompts return zero recommendations, and what do the no-slash penalty and the mutating-command gate cost in recall versus what they buy in precision?\",\"What must the advisor_recommend output contract carry (kind, runnable, brief wording, token budget) for a model to act on a surfaced command instead of a raw bridge id?\",\"Which commands are safe to start without asking, which need a question first, and where should that run-or-ask policy live?\",\"Can a model start a slash command by itself on Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Devin and DSH, and what fallback exists where it cannot?\",\"Which mechanism actually brings a plain-chat request onto the command workflow on every runtime: advisor brief, AGENTS.md gate, hook, skill-to-command pointer, or runner refusal?\",\"Which command workflows never load the mode SKILL.md their metadata names, and should a skill recommendation imply its command?\",\"Which benchmark rows and metrics separate a missed command from a wrongly st...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/iterations/iteration-001.md:\n  Line 14: 3. Five shipped identifiers are absent from the projection under their own names: /local-skilled-alignment, /prompt:improve, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save and /speckit:search. The allow-list keeps /prompt and /memory:save aliases, so exact-name absence does not prove that every related workflow is unreachable. Three projected names have no matching command file: /memory:save, /prompt and deprecated /spec_kit. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/prompt/improve.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/search.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:31-57]\n\n  Line 50: - .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/deltas/iter-001.jsonl:\n  Line 1: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-codex-luna-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-codex-luna-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-codex-luna-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"executor\":{\"kind\":\"cli-codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"serviceTier\":\"fast\",\"sandboxMode\":\"workspace-write\"},\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Angle 1: Inventory, reconcile the 45 command files with bridge sources and runtime-enabled bridge identities.\",\"focusTrack\":\"inventory\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.42,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Two of six findings are new, one extends an existing grouping-key model, and three reproduce the prior checked inventory; (2 + 0.5) / 6 rounds to 0.42.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which one canonical inventory reconciles command metadata, active bridge allow-list rows and doctor routing declarations for all 45 slash commands?\",\"How should command intent and skill intent combine so plain planning and research prompts reach the matching workflow with acceptable recall and precision?\",\"What should a command recommendation show, and which commands can the model invoke directly versus asking first?\",\"How does a plain chat request reach the appropriate command workflow across supported runtimes, and how should skills link to command front doors?\",\"What benchmark evidence, prior art and failure controls should validate the design?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"Recursive markdown count as the command denominator, because nested doctor fixtures inflate it.\",\"Treating generated bridge rows as unique commands, because several command strings have multiple route or compatibility rows.\",\"Treating legacy aliases as proof that a shipped command is represented by its own command identifier.\"],\"edgeCase\":\"ambiguous-input\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/comm...\n  Line 4: {\"id\":\"f-iter001-003\",\"label\":\"Five shipped command identifiers are absent from the bridge projection under their own names: /local-skilled-alignment, /prompt:improve, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save and /speckit:search. The /prompt and /memory:save aliases may reach two of those on some scoring surfaces, so absence by exact command identifier does not prove total unreachability. Three projected names have no matching command file: /memory:save, /prompt and deprecated /spec_kit.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md\",\".skilled/commands/prompt/improve.md\",\".skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md\",\".skilled/commands/speckit/save.md\",\".skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\"],\"type\":\"finding\"}\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/findings-registry.json:\n  Line 156:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\n\n  Line 174:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\n\n  Line 186:       \"text\": \"Five shipped identifiers are absent from the projection under their own names: /local-skilled-alignment, /prompt:improve, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save and /speckit:search. The allow-list keeps /prompt and /memory:save aliases, so exact-name absence does not prove that every related workflow is unreachable. Three projected names have no matching command file: /memory:save, /prompt and deprecated /spec_kit. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/prompt/improve.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/save.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/search.md:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:31-57]\",\n\n  Line 192:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\n\n  Line 210:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\n\n  Line 228:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\n\n  Line 246:         \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/codex-luna/state-events/iter-001.json:\n  Line 1: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-codex-luna-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-codex-luna-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-codex-luna-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"executor\":{\"kind\":\"cli-codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoningEffort\":\"max\",\"serviceTier\":\"fast\",\"sandboxMode\":\"workspace-write\"},\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Angle 1: Inventory, reconcile the 45 command files with bridge sources and runtime-enabled bridge identities.\",\"focusTrack\":\"inventory\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.42,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Two of six findings are new, one extends an existing grouping-key model, and three reproduce the prior checked inventory; (2 + 0.5) / 6 rounds to 0.42.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which one canonical inventory reconciles command metadata, active bridge allow-list rows and doctor routing declarations for all 45 slash commands?\",\"How should command intent and skill intent combine so plain planning and research prompts reach the matching workflow with acceptable recall and precision?\",\"What should a command recommendation show, and which commands can the model invoke directly versus asking first?\",\"How does a plain chat request reach the appropriate command workflow across supported runtimes, and how should skills link to command front doors?\",\"What benchmark evidence, prior art and failure controls should validate the design?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"Recursive markdown count as the command denominator, because nested doctor fixtures inflate it.\",\"Treating generated bridge rows as unique commands, because several command strings have multiple route or compatibility rows.\",\"Treating legacy aliases as proof that a shipped command is represented by its own command identifier.\"],\"edgeCase\":\"ambiguous-input\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/comm...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/resource-map.md:\n  Line 77: | .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json | Cited | OK | Citations=2; Iterations=2 |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:\n  Line 10: - Read the three `command-metadata.json` files (system-deep-loop, sk-design, sk-doc) and the bridge `allow-list.json`.\n\n  Line 21: 3. Four live grouped commands have no generated bridge at all: `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:handoff`, `/speckit:save`, and `/speckit:search`. The allow-list explains two adjacent gaps: `/speckit:*` commands exist only because `system-spec-kit` \"has no command-metadata.json yet\", and `/prompt` is bridged under its retired spelling while \"JSON declares `/prompt:improve`\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:52] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:7]\n\n  Line 23: 4. Three generated bridges name spellings that are not live grouped commands: `/spec_kit` is explicitly \"deprecated ... one-release compatibility\", `/memory:save` is retained as a legacy scorer key, and `/prompt` is the legacy name for `/prompt:improve`. A bridge can therefore outlive the command it names, and the projection does not flag that drift. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:35] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:49] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:56]\n\n  Line 53: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:3-56`\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:\n  Line 21: 3. A typed slash command is the only path that reliably activates the planning bridge: `/speckit:plan a new feature for the login page` returns `command-spec-kit` and `system-spec-kit`, both at 0.82. The bridge's entire keyword and intent-signal set is four slash markers (`/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:resume`, `/deep:research`, `/deep:review`), so it carries no plain-language planning phrase that a chat prompt could match. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:3] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:80]\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out:\n  Line 5: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476137871,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_9986fffa21d8415997ebf11d\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/spec.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: ---\\n2: title: \\\"Feature Specification: Research how the skill advisor should surface slash commands and how native chat reaches the proper command workflow without the user typing a command\\\"\\n3: description: \\\"The advisor recommends skills but surfaces only doctor commands as runnable lines, and plain chat prompts for planning or research get no recommendation at all. This packet researches how every command gets surfaced and how a chat-only user still lands on the proper command workflow.\\\"\\n4: trigger_phrases:\\n5:   - \\\"command surfacing and workflow enforcement\\\"\\n6:   - \\\"research how the skill advisor should surface slash\\\"\\n7: importance_tier: \\\"normal\\\"\\n8: contextType: \\\"general\\\"\\n9: ---\\n10: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\\n11: # Feature Specification: Research how the skill advisor should surface slash commands and how native chat reaches the proper command workflow without the user typing a command\\n12: \\n13: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\\n14: ---\\n15: \\n16: <!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\\n17: ## 1. METADATA\\n18: \\n19: | Field | Value |\\n20: |-------|-------|\\n21: | **Level** | 1 |\\n22: | **Priority** | P1 |\\n23: | **Status** | Draft |\\n24: | **Created** | 2026-11-12 |\\n25: | **Branch** | `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research` |\\n26: <!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\\n27: \\n28: ---\\n29: \\n30: <!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\\n31: ## 2. PROBL...\n  Line 43: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476257012,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_17a19da38ba34fb6b2bb1456\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Command Surfacing and Workflow Enforcement\\ndescription: Runtime strategy file for the opencode-deepseek lineage researching advisor command surfacing and chat-only routing.\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"command surfacing strategy\\\"\\n  - \\\"deep research strategy\\\"\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - Command Surfacing and Workflow Enforcement\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the opencode-deepseek fan-out lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next across 10 iterations.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** populated Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config.\\n- **Per iteration:** agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes machine-owned sections.\\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nHow should the skill advisor surface slash commands (all 45 under .skilled/commands, not only /doctor) so a model either runs the matching command workflow by itself or asks the user first, and how does a request typed as plain chat with no slash command still reach the proper command workflow on every runtime?\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through the research/inbox.jsonl surface.\\n\\n- [ ] Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what does one drift-proof command inventory need?\\n- [ ] Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do t...\n  Line 54: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476292364,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_8b2f3a3ed702463db61f1910\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"find .skilled -name \\\"command-metadata.json\\\" -not -path \\\"*/node_modules/*\\\"; echo \\\"---ALLOWLIST---\\\"; find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor -name \\\"allow-list.json\\\" -not -path \\\"*/node_modules/*\\\"; echo \\\"---ADVISOR SRC---\\\"; find .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor -maxdepth 3 -type d -not -path \\\"*/node_modules*\\\" -not -path \\\"*/changelog*\\\" | sort | head -40\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"},\"output\":\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/command-metadata.json\\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/command-metadata.json\\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json\\n---ALLOWLIST---\\n.skilled