mly by every scoring surface. The deriver combines live skill metadata with the authored compatibility inputs and wr...\n  Line 78: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476361800,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_01_9f7wip7lpcermyuh9nxah0b3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"doctorRoutes\\\\|typescriptActive\\\\|pythonActive\\\\|entries\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json | head -8; echo \\\"---DERIVE-HEAD---\\\"; grep -n \\\"allow-list\\\\|command-metadata\\\\|_routes\\\\|scoring-compatibility\\\\|commandBridges\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs | head -30; echo \\\"---006/003-PRIOR---\\\"; ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/ | head -20; echo \\\"---003-RESEARCH---\\\"; ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/003-doctor-command-surfacing/research/ 2>/dev/null | head\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"},\"output\":\"7:    \\\"doctorRoutes\\\": 35,\\n9:    \\\"typescriptActive\\\": 40,\\n10:    \\\"pythonActive\\\": 50\\n12:  \\\"entries\\\": [\\n---DERIVE-HEAD---\\n21:const ALLOW_LIST_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'allow-list.json');\\n23:const DOCTOR_ROUTES_PATH = join(DOCTOR_COMMANDS_DIR, '_routes.yaml');\\n24:const COMPATIBILITY_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'scoring-compatibility.json');\\n87:    const filePath = join(skillsRoot, skillId, 'command-metadata.json');\\n119:    throw new Error('[command-bridges] allow-list.json must contain a JSON array');\\n123:      throw new Error(`[command-bridges] allow-list.json[${index}] must be an object`);\\n128:        `[command-bridges] allow-list.json[${index}] requires id, command, skillId, ownerMode, and reason`,\\n136:      source: 'scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json',\\n178:    throw new Error('[command-bridges] _routes.yaml routes must be an array');\\n181:    doctorCommandName(route.command, `_routes.yaml routes[${index}]`)\\n190:    const label = `_routes.yaml routes[${index}]`;\\n221:    throw new Error('[co...\n  Line 85: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476380551,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_00_liyi9v9krhd8np8qo1knlhdu\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"id\\\\|command\\\\|reason\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json; echo \\\"---README-LINES---\\\"; grep -n \\\"third source\\\\|one bridge per doctor route\\\\|The deriver combines\\\\|activation\\\\|Activation\\\\|active\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md | head -20; echo \\\"---GEN-COUNT-LINES---\\\"; sed -n '1,14p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"},\"output\":\"3:    \\\"id\\\": \\\"command-spec-kit-plan\\\",\\n4:    \\\"command\\\": \\\"/speckit:plan\\\",\\n7:    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"system-spec-kit owns the live planning command but has no command-metadata.json yet.\\\"\\n10:    \\\"id\\\": \\\"command-spec-kit-complete\\\",\\n11:    \\\"command\\\": \\\"/speckit:complete\\\",\\n14:    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"system-spec-kit owns the live completion command but has no command-metadata.json yet.\\\"\\n17:    \\\"id\\\": \\\"command-spec-kit-implement\\\",\\n18:    \\\"command\\\": \\\"/speckit:implement\\\",\\n21:    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"system-spec-kit owns the live implementation command but has no command-metadata.json yet.\\\"\\n24:    \\\"id\\\": \\\"command-spec-kit-resume\\\",\\n25:    \\\"command\\\": \\\"/speckit:resume\\\",\\n28:    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"system-spec-kit owns the live resume command but has no command-metadata.json yet.\\\"\\n31:    \\\"id\\\": \\\"command-spec-kit\\\",\\n32:    \\\"command\\\": \\\"/spec_kit\\\",\\n35:    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The deprecated generic Spec Kit bridge remains live for one-release compatibility and has no JSON command entry.\\\"\\n38:    \\\"id\\\": \\\"command-memory-save\\\",\\n39:    \\\"command\\\": \\\"/memory:save\\\",\\n42:    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"system-spec-kit owns memory persistence but has no command-metadata.json yet.\\...\n  Line 91: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476414912,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_7hc1fmh3w18unry1mlj0a3jk\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"# Iteration 1: Command inventory drift across three metadata sources\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 1 (inventory): which of the 45 commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what one drift-proof inventory needs. The selected interpretation of \\\"active bridge\\\" is a generated bridge entry that is enabled for at least one scoring platform, because the generated projection contains entries that neither scorer loads.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Enumerated every markdown command under `.skilled/commands` and separated grouped hub commands from the loose `local-skilled-alignment.md`.\\n- Read the three `command-metadata.json` files (system-deep-loop, sk-design, sk-doc) and the bridge `allow-list.json`.\\n- Read the doctor route manifest `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml`.\\n- Parsed `command-bridges.generated.json` and compared its 62 entries against the live command tree, including per-platform `enabled` flags.\\n- Read the bridge deriver and its README to establish which inputs are authoritative.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The live command surface is 45 markdown files: 44 grouped commands (13 `/create:*`, 3 `/deep:*`, 3 `/design:*`, 17 `/doctor:*`, 1 `/prompt:*`, 7 `/speckit:*`) plus the loose `local-skilled-alignment.md`. Only 19 of those commands appear in a `command-metadata.json`, because only three skill hubs publish command metadata: `system-deep-loop` (3 commands), `sk-design` (3), and `sk-doc` (13). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/command-metadata.json:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-design/command-metadata.json:1] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json:1]\\n\\n2. The generated bridge projection holds 62 entries sourced from 19 command-metadata rows, 8 allow-list rows, and 35 doctor routes, but those 62 entries...\n  Line 97: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476436155,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_deeowi9e0x0c7f9qmoafuv84\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"run\\\":1,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Command inventory drift across three metadata sources\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":7,\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.95,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Seven findings are all new to this lineage; the 0.95 discount reflects partial overlap with the sibling 003 doctor-surfacing packet.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what does one drift-proof command inventory need?\\\",\\\"Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do the no-slash penalty and mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what does one drift-proof command inventory need?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"Counting generated bridge entries as commands\\\",\\\"Treating the allow-list as a complete fallback\\\"],\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"Glob\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\".skilled/commands\\\",\\\"/skdills/system-deep-loop/command-metadata.json\\\".replace(\\\"/skdills\\\",\\\"/.skilled/skills\\\"),\\\".skilled/skills/sk-design/command-metadata.json\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sys...\n  Line 175: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476632655,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_v87afxkaltx4ysvbjtc3451v\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"# Iteration 2: Why plain planning and research prompts score zero\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 2 (scoring): why plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how command intent competes with skill intent in fusion, and what the no-slash penalty and the mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Reproduced the two measured prompts from `spec.md` and captured the full candidate list with a lowered threshold.\\n- Read the fusion ranking, confidence calibration, and recommendation threshold code.\\n- Read the command-bridge projection to check whether `/deep:research` and `/speckit:plan` are routable descriptors.\\n- Read the deriver's read-only route classification.\\n- Ran three contrast prompts: literal slash, workflow wording without a slash, and a read-only planning question.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The default confidence threshold is 0.8 with a 0.35 uncertainty ceiling. For \\\"plan a new feature for the login page\\\" the complete candidate set is `sk-doc` at 0.6202, `sk-code` at 0.5923, and `system-spec-kit` at 0.5887, so every candidate fails the 0.8 bar and `advisor_recommend` returns an empty list. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/compat/contract.ts:9] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1245]\\n\\n2. For \\\"research how our retrieval scoring works in depth\\\" the candidates are `system-spec-kit` at 0.5874, `cli-external-orchestration` at 0.5759, and `sk-prompt` at 0.5747; the `/deep:research` bridge never enters the race because `command-deep-research` is projected with `routingEnabled: false`, empty keywords, empty intent signals, and empty domains. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts:1061]\\n\\n3. A typed s...\n  Line 181: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794476653650,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_e05eypsrrpw0f4oadc4nahd0\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"run\\\":2,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Scoring: why plain planning and research prompts return zero\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":7,\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.9,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"All seven findings are new to this lineage; the 0.9 discount reflects the scoring angle overlapping the inventory finding about inactive bridges.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do the no-slash penalty and mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision?\\\",\\\"What must the advisor render inside the 80 to 120 token brief for a model to act on a command, given that advisor_recommend has no kind or runnable field?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do the no-slash penalty and mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"Lowering the confidence threshold alone as the fix\\\",\\\"Treating the no-slash penalty as the cause of zero recommendations\\\"],\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"ambiguous-input\\\",\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/compat/contract.ts\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/...\n  Line 397: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794477416927,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e30e8da22ffebDKB2cyvqFU701\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_n0ryg5j1y2r3azhteqfcm0gv\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"# Command Surfacing and Chat-Only Workflow Enforcement: Research Synthesis\\n\\n> Lineage: `opencode-deepseek` | Iterations: 10 | Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` | Executor: `cli-opencode` / `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\nThe repository has two command-routing systems that do not meet. The command tree, the hub metadata and the module registries already describe every command and its owning mode. The advisor, however, scores skills and only renders a runnable command for the 17 `/doctor:*` routers. Every other command either arrives as a raw bridge id, is inactive in the TypeScript scorer, or never reaches the model. A plain-chat planning or research prompt returns zero recommendations at the shipped 0.8 threshold, so the user's request is answered by a hand-rolled workflow even when a command owns it.\\n\\nThe research supports a single recommendation with three parts:\\n\\n1. Build one command inventory from the command tree and the hub `mode-registry.json` files, with a completeness gate and a `safetyClass` per command.\\n2. Extend the recommendation payload and brief with `kind`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`; keep the existing 80/120 token budget and render the command for every family, not only doctor.\\n3. Put the enforcement sentence in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, where every runtime reads it, and keep the command document as the executable workflow body. No runtime exposes a model-callable slash command, so the model either loads and follows the command document or asks the user to type the command.\\n\\nNo change is recommended to how skills are scored against each other. Every finding below cites repository code or measured advisor output; the external prior art is cited to its official documentation.\\n\\...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/research.md:\n  Line 33: The generated bridge projection holds 62 entries from 19 metadata rows, 8 allow-list rows and 35 doctor routes, collapsing to 43 distinct command spellings. Four live grouped commands have no generated bridge: `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:handoff`, `/speckit:save` and `/speckit:search`. Three generated bridges name non-live spellings: `/spec_kit` (deprecated), `/memory:save` (legacy key) and `/prompt` (legacy name for `/prompt:improve`). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json:4] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:35]\n\n  Line 39: **Recommendation R1.** Build the inventory from `.skilled/commands` plus each hub's `mode-registry.json`, and make the deriver fail when a live command is missing from both. Keep `allow-list.json` only for commands whose owner hub genuinely has no metadata, and make every entry expire with the command file.\n\n  Line 47: A typed `/speckit:plan` prompt returns `command-spec-kit` and `system-spec-kit` at 0.82, but the bridge's entire keyword set is four slash markers (`/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:resume`, `/deep:research`, `/deep:review`). It has no plain-language planning phrase. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:3]\n\n  Line 241: | Treat `allow-list.json` as the fallback inventory | It covers 8 commands, misses four live commands and adds three retired aliases. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:52] |\n\n  Line 283: - `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json`\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-001.jsonl:\n  Line 1: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Command inventory drift across three metadata sources\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":0.95,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Seven findings are all new to this lineage; the 0.95 discount reflects partial overlap with the sibling 003 doctor-surfacing packet.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what does one drift-proof command inventory need?\",\"Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do the no-slash penalty and mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Which commands have no active bridge, which bridges point at retired names, and what does one drift-proof command inventory need?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Counting generated bridge entries as commands\",\"Treating the allow-list as a complete fallback\"],\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Glob\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/commands\",\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/sk-design/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/command-metadata.json\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\",\".skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T09:40:24Z\",\"durationMs\":...\n  Line 4: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-003\",\"label\":\"Four live grouped commands have no generated bridge: /prompt:improve, /speckit:handoff, /speckit:save and /speckit:search; the allow-list bridges /prompt under its retired spelling.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:52\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:7\"]}\n\n  Line 5: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-004\",\"label\":\"Three generated bridges name non-live spellings: /spec_kit is deprecated, /memory:save is a retained legacy key and /prompt is the legacy name for /prompt:improve.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:35\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:49\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/allow-list.json:56\"]}\n\n  Line 10: {\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Treating allow-list.json as a complete fallback inventory\",\"reason\":\"It covers 8 commands, misses four live commands and adds three retired aliases\",\"iteration\":1}\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/007-command-surfacing-and-workflow-enforcement/research/lineages/opencode-deepseek/deltas/iter-002.jsonl:\n  Line 1: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"run\":2,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-deepseek-1794475749931-e4ukfw\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Scoring: why plain planning and research prompts return zero\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All seven findings are new to this lineage; the 0.9 discount reflects the scoring angle overlapping the inventory finding about inactive bridges.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Why do plain planning and research prompts return no recommendation, how does command intent compete with skill intent in fusion, and what do the no-slash penalty and mutating-command gate cost in recall versus precision?\",\"What must the advisor render inside the 80 to 120 token brief for a model to act on 